  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-5}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-5\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
